 "_note": "One entry per jurisdiction, read by every news module through news/jurisdictions.mjs. Chamber names are the short forms a card uses (\"House\" for a House of Representatives or House of Delegates; New Jersey's lower chamber is the General Assembly). unicameral: the one body's name (then upper/lower are null). executive: who acts on a passed measure. news_executive_wording false (review r6 #7, deliberate): the territories have governors, but a card names no executive and makes no law claim except a became-law record with valid law wording, because their signing flows are not modelled. law_wording false (review r4 #4): a District act becomes law only after Congressional review, so no 'into law' wording. Bill-number prefixes: state_prefixes apply to every jurisdiction unless default_prefixes is false; a jurisdiction's own prefixes override them. Each prefix: chamber (upper | lower | null: the number does not say), kind (bill | resolution | constitutional amendment), simple (one chamber's own resolution), skips_executive (default: true for every resolution and amendment, false for a bill).",
